.TH SAPHIRA-INSTALL-PLAN 8 "Saphira Linux" "Installation planner"
.SH NAME
saphira-install-plan \- validate and display a Saphira installation manifest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-install-plan validate|show
.I MANIFEST
.RB [ --kernel-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --profile-root
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR saphira-install-plan
is the declarative front end of Saphira installation. A manifest file
(see
.BR saphira-install-plan (5))
describes the whole installation; this tool validates it
.RB ( validate )
or prints the human-readable plan with storage sketch, kernel
.BR needs :
lines and the destructive target warning
.RB ( show ).
It writes nothing, touches no disk and opens no network: the USB
installer, the future pre-boot menu and image creation share the
same format and the same refusals.
.PP
.B --kernel-config
points at a kernel
.I .config
so filesystem support is proven rather than assumed; without it the
plan reports support as unproven (ZFS additionally needs its
out-of-tree modules, which no
.I .config
can prove).
.B --profile-root
overrides the profile tree used to resolve
.BR PROFILE .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the manifest is valid; 1 with a refusal naming the exact
offense otherwise.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/saphira/install-manifest.example
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-install-plan (5),
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR saphira-install (8)
